---Data detailing messaging delivery
---@class gcp.fcmdata_v1beta1.GoogleFirebaseFcmDataV1beta1Data
---@field countNotificationsAccepted? string Count of notifications accepted by FCM intended for Android devices. The targeted device must have opted in to the collection of usage and diagnostic information.
---@field proxyNotificationInsightPercents? gcp.fcmdata_v1beta1.GoogleFirebaseFcmDataV1beta1ProxyNotificationInsightPercents Additional insights about proxy notification delivery.
---@field messageOutcomePercents? gcp.fcmdata_v1beta1.GoogleFirebaseFcmDataV1beta1MessageOutcomePercents Mutually exclusive breakdown of message delivery outcomes.
---@field deliveryPerformancePercents? gcp.fcmdata_v1beta1.GoogleFirebaseFcmDataV1beta1DeliveryPerformancePercents Additional information about delivery performance for messages that were successfully delivered.
---@field messageInsightPercents? gcp.fcmdata_v1beta1.GoogleFirebaseFcmDataV1beta1MessageInsightPercents Additional general insights about message delivery.
---@field countMessagesAccepted? string Count of messages accepted by FCM intended for Android devices. The targeted device must have opted in to the collection of usage and diagnostic information.

---Overview of delivery performance for messages that were successfully delivered. All percentages are calculated with countMessagesAccepted as the denominator. These categories are not mutually exclusive; a message can be delayed for multiple reasons.
---@class gcp.fcmdata_v1beta1.GoogleFirebaseFcmDataV1beta1DeliveryPerformancePercents
---@field delayedDeviceDoze? number The percentage of accepted messages that were delayed because the device was in doze mode. Only [normal priority messages](https://firebase.google.com/docs/cloud-messaging/concept-options#setting-the-priority-of-a-message) should be delayed due to doze mode.
---@field delayedUserStopped? number The percentage of accepted messages that were delayed because the intended device user-profile was [stopped](https://firebase.google.com/docs/cloud-messaging/android/receive#handling_messages) on the target device at the time of the send. The messages were eventually delivered when the user-profile was started again.
---@field delayedMessageThrottled? number The percentage of accepted messages that were delayed due to message throttling, such as [collapsible message throttling](https://firebase.google.com/docs/cloud-messaging/concept-options#collapsible_throttling).
---@field deliveredNoDelay? number The percentage of accepted messages that were delivered to the device without delay from the FCM system.
---@field delayedDeviceOffline? number The percentage of accepted messages that were delayed because the target device was not connected at the time of sending. These messages were eventually delivered when the device reconnected.

